WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:19.067
Simon Lab is where your agent works:
a CLI and a toolset for building complete

2
00:00:19.134 --> 00:00:21.044
chemical-engineering projects,

3
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.731
layer by layer, starting from the physics
that governs the process and adding detail

4
00:00:25.798 --> 00:00:29.736
at every stage. The agent
begins with the spec: scope,

5
00:00:29.803 --> 00:00:33.536
capacity and economics, in CapacityIndex.

6
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.612
In ProcessView, the agent builds the P&amp;ID.

7
00:00:37.679 --> 00:00:40.874
Every line, valve and instrument
carries its full selection,

8
00:00:40.941 --> 00:00:43.567
materials, pipe classes,
nozzles, parameters,

9
00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:47.925
plus guidelines for mechanical design,
instrumentation and control.

10
00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:51.183
The schematic runs as
a dynamic process simulation:

11
00:00:51.249 --> 00:00:53.470
filling, mixing, dosing, cooling,

12
00:00:53.536 --> 00:00:55.679
proven before you buy a single pipe.

13
00:00:56.125 --> 00:01:00.172
Ready-made control programs
run on an emulated PLC.

14
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.367
The parameters flow into MechGraph, where
the machine is designed from dedicated

15
00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:10.283
calculations: mixing power
and solids suspension,

16
00:01:10.358 --> 00:01:15.728
shaft deflection and critical speed,
strength, and CFD simulation.

17
00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:20.655
In parallel, IonGrid turns the control
logic into real cabinets built from

18
00:01:20.721 --> 00:01:22.060
catalog components,

19
00:01:22.126 --> 00:01:27.089
with heat-gain balance, pneumatic
control and a purchase list.

20
00:01:28.433 --> 00:01:31.678
PlantMesh builds complete
process-unit assemblies:

21
00:01:32.032 --> 00:01:35.913
piping isometrics, support
structures with FEM analysis,

22
00:01:35.979 --> 00:01:40.711
service access, cable routing
and automatic clash detection.

23
00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:45.554
Architecture places the unit in your
plant: terrain from public geospatial

24
00:01:45.621 --> 00:01:49.304
data, point clouds from
scans of existing facilities,

25
00:01:49.371 --> 00:01:50.534
roads and buildings,

26
00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:52.848
all the way to the site plan.

27
00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:59.024
A full export of
construction-ready documentation,

28
00:01:59.471 --> 00:02:03.505
from a tested process and
a clash-checked 3D model.

29
00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:10.576
Simon Lab. Bottom-up chemical engineering.

30
00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.979
Now in beta with trusted partners.
